    "The MMLU benchmark is a systematic test for measuring how much factual and world knowledge a large language model has learned.",
    "It was introduced in 2020.",
    "It consists of about 14,000 multiple‑choice questions spread across roughly 57 different subjects.",
    "The subjects range from math and science to humanities and social sciences.",
    "By asking a model to answer each question and recording the percentage of correct responses, researchers can gauge the breadth of knowledge the model has retained from its training data.",
    "Because the questions are publicly available, later models can become “contaminated” by having seen the questions during training.",
    "This contamination eventually leads to the benchmark becoming saturated and less useful for distinguishing newer models.",
    "Nonetheless, MMLU remains a foundational benchmark for evaluating LLM knowledge."
] 

